      <memberdef kind="variable" id="class_u_tryll_generate_and_speak_params_1a500b2dc826a6c64033cdd51d1d89787a" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>int32</type>
        <definition>int32 UTryllGenerateAndSpeakParams::FirstChunkMaxChars</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>FirstChunkMaxChars</name>
        <qualifiedname>UTryllGenerateAndSpeakParams::FirstChunkMaxChars</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= 0</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Time-to-first-audio knob. When &gt; 0, the FIRST chunk may also end at a comma, semicolon or colon followed by a space, or at an em dash, and is cut at the next space once it is this wide, so speech starts sooner. Neither cut fires before 5 words or min_sentence_chars. Later chunks keep whole sentences. No effect on text without spaces (CJK). 0 = off. 48 is the measured starting point: about 40% less model-side wait on Supertonic and Pocket. Check how it sounds with your voice before shipping it. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
